<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Ledgerly | Know where your naira goes</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Track income and spending in naira, set budgets and savings goals, and follow crypto and stock prices in one place.">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,400;12..96,600;12..96,800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css">
</head>
<body class="home">
  <header class="home-nav">
    <a class="brand" href="/">Ledgerly</a>
    <nav class="home-nav-links" aria-label="Main">
      <% if (loggedIn) { %>
        <a class="btn gold" href="/dashboard">Open dashboard</a>
      <% } else { %>
        <a class="btn ghost-light" href="/login">Log in</a>
        <a class="btn gold" href="/register">Create account</a>
      <% } %>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <h1>Know where your naira goes.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Record what comes in and what goes out, set limits before you overspend, save towards what matters, and watch crypto and stock prices, all in one place.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <% if (loggedIn) { %>
          <a class="btn gold big" href="/dashboard">Go to your dashboard</a>
        <% } else { %>
          <a class="btn gold big" href="/register">Start tracking, it's free</a>
          <a class="btn ghost-light big" href="/login">I have an account</a>
        <% } %>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sheet" role="img" aria-label="Example of a Ledgerly dashboard with a balance, three transactions and a food budget">
      <div class="sheet-balance">
        <span>Total balance</span>
        <strong>₦184,500.00</strong>
      </div>
      <ul class="sheet-rows">
        <li><span>Allowance</span><span class="pos">+₦60,000.00</span></li>
        <li><span>Food</span><span class="neg">-₦12,800.00</span></li>
        <li><span>Data &amp; airtime</span><span class="neg">-₦3,500.00</span></li>
        <li><span>School fees</span><span class="neg">-₦45,000.00</span></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="sheet-budget">
        <div class="top"><span>Food budget</span><span>₦12,800 of ₦20,000</span></div>
        <div class="bar"><span style="width:64%"></span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sheet-note">Sample data</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>What you can do with it</h2>
    <div class="feature-list">
      <article>
        <h3>Track every naira</h3>
        <p>Add income and spending in seconds, sort them into categories like food, transport and school fees, and search or edit them later.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Stay inside your budget</h3>
        <p>Set a monthly limit for each category. You get a warning at 80% and a clear alert when you go over.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Save towards goals</h3>
        <p>Name what you are saving for, set a target and a deadline, and see how much to put aside each month.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Follow the markets</h3>
        <p>Chart crypto and US stocks over the last month to year, and keep a watchlist of the ones you care about.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Record your investments</h3>
        <p>Log what you bought and at what price. Your portfolio shows its current value and your gain or loss.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <h3>Take it with you</h3>
        <p>Download a PDF report for any month, or export all your transactions to a spreadsheet.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section steps-section">
    <h2>Up and running in three steps</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li><strong>Create an account.</strong> It takes a minute and needs only your name, email and a password.</li>
      <li><strong>Record your money.</strong> Add your allowance or salary, then log spending as it happens.</li>
      <li><strong>Check your month.</strong> Open the dashboard to see where it went, and download your report.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <h2>Start with this month.</h2>
    <% if (loggedIn) { %>
      <a class="btn gold big" href="/dashboard">Open dashboard</a>
    <% } else { %>
      <a class="btn gold big" href="/register">Create your free account</a>
    <% } %>
  </section>
  
  <section class="section">
    <h2>Questions people ask</h2>
    <div class="faq">
      <details>
        <summary>Does Ledgerly connect to my bank account?</summary>
        <p>No. You record your income and spending yourself, so nothing is shared with your bank and no card details are ever needed.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is my data private?</summary>
        <p>Each account only sees its own records. Passwords are stored in scrambled (hashed) form, and you can export or delete your entries at any time.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Does it cost anything?</summary>
        <p>No. Creating an account and using every feature is free.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Where do the crypto and stock prices come from?</summary>
        <p>Crypto prices come from CoinPaprika and stock prices from Tiingo. Prices are in US dollars, may be delayed, and are for information only, not investment advice.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I track Nigerian stocks?</summary>
        <p>Not yet. The market charts cover crypto and US stocks and ETFs. Your income, spending, budgets and savings goals are all in naira.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I use it on my phone?</summary>
        <p>Yes. The pages adjust to any screen size, so you can use it in your phone's browser.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="home-footer">
    <span>Ledgerly, a final year project.</span>
    <span>Market prices are in US dollars, may be delayed, and are not investment advice.</span>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>